plied by controller name; included for DSC and component controllers in the same pass as a queryability enhancement)\n- Migrate DSCI controller structured keys from \"Request.Name\"/\"DSCInitialization\" to \"name\"/\"namespace\"\n- Cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit name and resourceKind; namespace omitted or empty, never spurious\n- Unit tests parsing test logger output asserting field presence/correctness for service controllers, module controller handlers, and all 15 action files; DSCI standard field names; cluster-scoped behavior\n- CI lint/static-analysis check wired into CI for the manager binary, flagging log.Error calls that embed name/namespace in message text or omit required structured fields\n- Backwards-compatibility validation: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured (Loki), trigger reconciliation errors, verify ingestion without configuration changes\n- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on changed message-string patterns and document required updates\n- Message strings updated to remove redundant resource identity moved to structured fields\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n1. A complete audit checklist of every log.Error() reconciliation-error call site in the manager binary exists (produced by grep/static analysis), with each site marked converted or not-applicable.\n2. Given a manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when updated, the call uses structured key-value pairs (\"name\", \"namespace\") — measured by the CI lint rule flagging zero remaining log.Error calls with identity embedded in message text in manager binary sources.\n3. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert that service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) error logs include \"resourceKind\" with the correct value.\n4. Unit tests assert all 15 action files' error logs (8 component: components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go; 3 service: services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go; 1 DSC: datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go; 3 module: modules/modules_controller_actions*.go) include \"name\", \"namespace\", and \"resourceKind\" with correct values.\n5. DSCI controller error logs use camelCase field names (\"name\", \"namespace\", \"resourceKind\"); a unit test asserts the standard names and a codebase grep confirms no remaining \"Request.Name\"/\"DSCInitialization\" field usage in the DSCI controller.\n6. Unit tests assert cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit \"name\" and \"resourceKind\" with namespace omitted or empty — no spurious namespace value.\n7. Module controller error logs include \"name\", \"namespace\", \"resourceKind\" across all 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator) — unit test.\n8. DSC and component controller error logs include \"resourceKind\" (bundled P1 from the same call-site pass).\n9. The lint/static-analysis check runs in CI for the manager binary and flags log.Error calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n10. Before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows structured fields present, and a dev-cluster test build with the production log consumer stack ingests both formats without configuration changes, verified before merge.\n11. Text-based alert rules affected by changed message strings are identified with SRE/Support and an update plan is documented before merge.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n- HLR-1 (P0): ... converts embedded identity to structured KV (manager binary scope)\n- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI migration\n- HLR-3 (P0): service controllers resourceKind\n- HLR-4 (P0): action files\n- HLR-6 (P0): module control