{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8b556e10-6b71-4202-b99b-55000ba0781a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82042a4069247a6f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-zaz9tdba/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n\n## Description\n\nAuthors the structured log field convention as a contribution guideline for new\ncontroller development in the rhods-operator, and publishes it as a specification for\nvoluntary adoption by external operator teams — the Cluster Observability Operator\nteam's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator — per platform policy (overlay 0008: RHOAI\ndoes not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies). The guideline\ncaptures the three-problem diagnosis behind the standardization (message-embedded\nidentity, non-standard DSCI key names, missing `resourceKind`) and the camelCase field\nconvention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) aligned with controller-runtime\npractice.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Contribution guideline for new controller development specifying:\n  - the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`);\n  - the camelCase naming rationale and its alignment with controller-runtime's\n    structured log key conventions;\n  - the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys,\n    missing `resourceKind`);\n  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded resource identity to\n    structured key-value pairs;\n  - the treatment of cluster-scoped resources (`namespace` omitted or empty).\n- DSCI key-name migration guide for operators: before/after query examples for\n  existing Loki/CloudWatch queries filtering on the retired `Request.Name` /\n  `DSCInitialization` field names, and release-notes documentation so the transition\n  lands in a single release.\n- Publish the convention as a specification for external operator adoption and file\n  tracking issues in the Cluster Observability Operator projects (Loki Operator,\n  Tempo Operator); adoption remains at their discretion per platform policy.\n- Record the PM/Observability team decision on whether the convention should include\n  fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error\n  category) and the associated log-volume trade-off.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields (`name`,\n   `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the\n   three-problem diagnosis, with before/after code examples for converting\n   message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n2. The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented manager-binary and\n   cloudmanager conversions, and the review sign-off is recorded.\n3. The DSCI key-name migration is documented with before/after query examples for\n   affected log queries, and the release-notes entry targets a single release.\n4. The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are\n   filed in the Cluster Observability Operator projects (Loki Operator, Tempo\n   Operator).\n5. The PM/Observability decision on additional fields beyond name/namespace/kind is\n   recorded in the guideline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P1): document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n  development and publish it for external operator adoption.\n\n## Notes\n\n- External adoption by the Cluster Observability Operator team is best-effort and\n  outside RHOAI control per platform policy; publishing early and filing tracking\n  issues is the mitigation for adoption delay.\n- The guideline documents what was built, so it is authored after the manager-binary\n  and cloudmanager conversions complete and is technically reviewed against them.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":69226,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8972947215b9907","agent_id":"a101f61d943c34416","session_id":"f64427cd-cf3e-4bee-9716-c63ae53a7129","uuid":"2200ff47-ca9a-4414-955e-bb091a7556b4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:38:36.916Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
