{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dc5afc478f83d83","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tConverts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and adds\n35\tthe `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error log calls in the rhods-operator\n36\tmanager binary, and migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard\n37\tkey names to the camelCase convention. The manager binary contains five controller\n38\ttiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers\n39\t(DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer,\n40\tTrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers\n41\t(Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator,\n42\tMCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth,\n43\tMonitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus 15 action files across four tiers\n44\t(8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module) that contain reconciliation logic invoked\n45\tduring reconciliation. Field naming follows controller-runtime's camelCase convention:\n46\t`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Audit every `log.Error()` call site in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n51\t  binary (all five controller tiers and all 15 action files) using grep/static\n52\t  analysis, and produce a coverage checklist marking each site converted or\n53\t  not-applicable.\n54\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string,\n55\t  extract the identity fields and convert them to structured key-value pairs\n56\t  (`\"name\"`, `\"namespace\"`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n57\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all\n58\t  controllers and action files. It is a functional requirement for service\n59\t  controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and action files (where the\n60\t  kind is not implied by the controller name), and a cross-controller queryability\n61\t  enhancement for the DSC and component controllers that is included in the same\n62\t  call-site pass.\n63\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured keys from the non-standard\n64\t  `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`.\n65\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit\n66\t  `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never\n67\t  a spurious value.\n68\t- Add unit tests that parse test logger output and assert field presence and\n69\t  correctness for the service controllers, the module controller and its handlers,\n70\t  all 15 action files, the DSCI standard field names, and the cluster-scoped\n71\t  behavior.\n72\t- Add a lint/static-analysis check, wired into CI for the manager binary, that flags\n73\t  `log.Error` calls embedding name/namespace in message text or missing the required\n74\t  structured fields.\n75\t- Backwards-compatibility validation: produce a before/after log output comparison\n76\t  for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the\n77\t  production log consumer stack configured (Loki), trigger reconciliation errors,\n78\t  and verify both log formats are ingested without configuration changes.\n79\t- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the\n80\t  changed message-string patterns and document the required updates.\n81\t\n82\tAction files in scope (15 total): 8 component action files\n83\t(`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n84\t(`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file\n85\t(`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module action\n86\tfiles (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n87\t\n88\t## Acceptance Criteria\n89\t\n90\t1. A complete audit checklist of every `log.Error()` reconciliation-error call site\n91\t   in the manager binary exists (produced by grep/static analysis), with each site\n92\t   marked converted or not-applicable.\n93\t2. Given a manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded\n94\t   resource name or namespace in the message string, the updated call uses structured\n95\t   key-value pairs (`\"name\"`, `\"namespace\"`) — measured by the CI lint rule reporting\n96\t   zero remaining `log.Error` calls with identity embedded in message text in manager\n97\t   binary sources.\n98\t3. Unit tests parsing test logger output assert that service controller (Gateway,\n99\t   Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) error logs include `resourceKind`\n100\t   with the correct value.\n101\t4. Unit tests assert that error logs in all 15 action files include `name`,\n102\t   `namespace`, and `resourceKind` with correct values.\n103\t5. DSCI controller error logs use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n104\t   `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting the standard field names and a\n105\t   codebase grep confirming no remaining `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` field\n106\t   usage in the DSCI controller.\n107\t6. Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources (DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization)\n108\t   emit `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty — no spurious\n109\t   namespace value.\n110\t7. Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across\n111\t   all 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches,\n112\t   MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator) — measured by unit test.\n113\t8. DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` for cross-controller\n114\t   queryability (P1 requirement delivered in the same call-site pass).\n115\t9. The lint/static-analysis check is wired into CI for the manager binary and flags\n116\t   `log.Error` calls that embed name/namespace in message text or omit required\n117\t   structured fields.\n118\t10. A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error shows the\n119\t    structured fields present, and a dev-cluster test build with the production log\n120\t    consumer stack ingests both formats without configuration changes — verified\n121\t    before merge.\n122\t11. Text-based alert rules affected by the changed message strings are identified\n123\t    together with SRE/Support and an update plan is documented before merge.\n124\t\n125\t## HLR Traceability\n126\t\n127\t- HLR-1 (P0): all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name\n128\t  or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs —\n129\t  manager binary scope of this requirement.\n130\t- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names\n131\t  (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention.\n132\t- HLR-3 (P0): service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator,\n133\t  Setup) reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n134\t- HLR-4 (P0): all action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n135\t  `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (15 action files).\n136\t- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and\n137\t  `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n138\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include\n139\t  `resourceKind` — bundled into this epic because it lands on the same `log.Error`\n140\t  call sites already restructured for HLR-1; a separate epic would force a second\n141\t  pass over the same files.\n142\t\n143\t## Risks\n144\t\n145\t- **Inconsistent adoption across controllers:** with five controller tiers and 15\n146\t  action files, some error paths may be missed — mitigated by the grep/static-analysis\n147\t  audit with a coverage checklist (AC 1) and the CI lint rule (AC 9).\n148\t- **Log consumer regression:** existing log consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) or text-based\n149\t  alert rules may fail on the new format — mitigated by the dev-cluster ingestion\n150\t  validation before merge (AC 10) and SRE/Support coordination (AC 11).\n151\t- **DSCI key name migration breaks existing queries:** operators may have queries\n152\t  filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` — the migration is documented with\n153\t  before/after query examples in the convention documentation and lands in a single\n154\t  release.\n155\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ce0563ea5245d8c","agent_id":"aedaccdf93b6b217c","session_id":"f64427cd-cf3e-4bee-9716-c63ae53a7129","uuid":"4b6a24f9-c7bc-4559-9512-e0553743edbb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:45:46.914Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dc5afc478f83d83","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 after revision"}
